From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m89wppy <zhalin66@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:37:09 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 41/42] BlueOS: wallpaper frames ~2x cheaper; the weather keeps
 moving while swiping; the jelly redraws only its box
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured on the phone (music, «Малооблачно», equalizer glow, a chibi): every wallpaper frame took ~11 ms of the
GPU — the surface is the picture's size (2400x3381) and each frame ran the weather's shaders on all of it, at the
equalizer's 30 fps; a jelly frame ran the scene twice more through a full-size effect at ~60 fps.
- Moving frames draw only the part of the surface the screen shows (the system only zooms in from there); the
  whole surface for the engine's own frames, the last frame before resting, the picker preview, a turned screen
  and with `setprop debug.blueos.wall.noclip 1`.
- The weather moves on at its own pace (rain / snow ~30 fps, clouds / fog / sun ~15 fps); frames in between
  (equalizer, jelly) show its last picture from a RenderNode layer.
- It no longer holds still while the launcher or the shade moves: it stopped and started with a jerk.
- The jelly redraws only the box its areas can reach (Sim.reach) through its effect, over the scene.
Wallpaper GPU time: idle 6.8 -> 3.4 s per 20 s, swiping 7.2 -> 3.5 s, jelly + swiping 11.5 -> 5.2 s; the
launcher's janky frames with the jelly 4.4 % -> 0 %, 95th percentile 53 -> 34 ms.

